  "title": "OpenBMI SSVEP EEG dataset (Lee et al. 2019)",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted derivative dataset of steady-state visually evoked potential (SSVEP) EEG recordings from 54 subjects across 2 sessions. The dataset contains 21,600 trials of 4-second EEG recordings at 1000 Hz sampling frequency from 62 channels, organized for standardized brain-computer interface benchmarking using the Mother of All BCI Benchmarks (MOABB) framework. This derivative was converted from the original Lee2019 source dataset using MNE-BIDS tools to enable reproducible analysis of SSVEP-based BCI paradigms.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data collected using SSVEP stimulation paradigm with 4-second trial duration at 1000 Hz sampling frequency across 62 channels. Data organized in BIDS format using MOABB pipeline and MNE-BIDS tools.",
